## Chapter 9 On-policy Prediction with Approximation

In this chapter, we begin our study of function approximation in reinforcement learning by considering its use in estimating the state-value function from on-policy data, that is, in approximating \(v_{\pi}\) from experience generated using a known policy \(\pi\). The novelty in this chapter is that the approximate value function is represented not as a table but as a parameterized functional form with weight vector \(\mathbf{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\). We will write \(\hat{v}(s,\mathbf{w})\approx v_{\pi}(s)\) for the approximate value of state \(s\) given weight vector \(\mathbf{w}\). For example, \(\hat{v}



